{
"meta": {
  "description": "Regional-variety marker inventory v0 for the corpus + model variety study (see DIALECT_EVAL.md). Codified standard-variety markers (DE/AT/CH) with lexical pairs, perfect-auxiliary grammar patterns, greetings, and CH orthography, plus dialect-tier hint markers (Bairisch/Schwiizerduetsch) used ONLY to annotate probe responses for manual review, never in headline counts.",
  "created": "2026-08-18",
  "freeze": "Frozen once the first scored run lands in DIALECT_EVAL.md. Later additions/pattern fixes go to variety_markers_v1.json so published numbers stay reproducible.",
  "citations": "AT lexis: Oesterreichisches Woerterbuch (44. Aufl.); Variantenwoerterbuch des Deutschen (2. Aufl., de Gruyter 2016). CH lexis + ss-orthography: Duden 'Schweizerhochdeutsch' (2012); the ss-for-eszett rule is official Swiss federal orthography. Aux-perfect variation (sitzen/stehen/liegen): Variantengrammatik des Standarddeutschen; Duden Bd. 9. DE-side 'Moin' is northern-German regional standard.",
  "matching": "All patterns are Python regexes applied with re.IGNORECASE to raw text. Word boundaries are explicit (?<!\\w)...(?!\\w) because Python treats umlauts and eszett as \\w (matching run_baseline_eval.py matches()); \\b would false-positive inside Ungeheuer, Semmelbroesel, heuern. Inflection is built into each pattern. compound_substring (lowercase substring) counts compound occurrences SEPARATELY: substring hits that are not standalone hits and not in compound_exclude. Ratios use standalone counts only.",
  "known_traps": [
    "Semmelbroesel/-knoedel/-mehl are pan-German cooking compounds, not AT markers (compound_exclude).",
    "'heuer' boundaries kill Ungeheuer/heuern/anheuern; a capitalized surname Heuer would still slip through (rare, sample-review).",
    "aux markers: 'mir ist daran gelegen' (stative, standard DE), adjectival 'zentral/ruhig gelegen' + sein (standard DE 'located'), and 'hat gestanden' = 'confessed' all inflate counts — the scan's --samples output exists to audit exactly these.",
    "aux gap excludes commas, so cross-clause bridging ('hat gesagt, dass sie dort gestanden ist') is not miscounted as haben-perfect; the cost is missing parenthetical commas inside one clause.",
    "'Grillen' (insect) collides with 'grillen' (verb) under IGNORECASE — noted, accepted for scan purposes.",
    "'weiss/Weiss' can be the surname Weiss (sample-review).",
    "'Brotzeit' as Jause-counterpart is itself southern-DE regional; Zwischenmahlzeit/Snack are the neutral forms."
  ]
},
"markers": [
  {"id": "lex-at-semmel", "variety": "AT", "tier": "standard", "category": "lexical", "gloss": "bread roll",
   "variant": {"label": "Semmel", "pattern": "(?<!\\w)(Semmeln?|Semmerln?)(?!\\w)"},
